      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "\"Permanent\" is a scary word, but it's also a lie we tell ourselves when we're too exhausted to imagine a different ending. You're not dragging a corpse—you're carrying a version of yourself that's still breathing, just barely, and that breath is enough to start again. And if fixing feels pointless, then don't fix—just exist for a while, without the pressure to be whole. The weight doesn't have to be carried all at once; you can set it down, even if it's just for a minute, and that's not giving up—that's surviving.",
